/* book exam traps: Do not set XL = XC at an arbitrary frequency. The equality XL = XC holds only at ω₀, so recompute both reactances whenever the source frequency changes. | In Q = ω₀L/R use ω₀ in rad/s, not f₀ in Hz. Using f₀ in place of ω₀ introduces a 2π error. | VL and VC cancel in the source loop, but each can be Q times the source voltage. Do not add their magnitudes as if they were in phase. | The half-power current is I₀/√2, about 0.707 I₀, not zero and not I₀. Half power means P/Pmax = 1/2. | At resonance the impedance is R, not zero. If R is very small, the ideal model predicts a very large current and very large VL and VC; real coils and sources always add some resistance. */
