/* book: lead: Parallel resonance happens when the capacitive and inductive susceptances in a parallel network are equal and opposite. They cancel, the tank looks purely resistive, and its impedance reaches a maximum. The supply then delivers minimum current, while the coil and capacitor exchange a much larger current between themselves. This idea sits inside every tuned radio stage, oscillator tank and filter t */
