/* book exam traps: Impedance is maximum at parallel resonance, not minimum. Series resonance gives minimum impedance and maximum supply current. | At resonance the supply current is small, but the coil and capacitor currents are large and opposite. Do not assume branch current is zero. | Parallel Q has R in the numerator: Q = R/(ω₀L). Do not invert the series formula blindly; the two use different resistances (the shunt R of an ideal tank, the series r of a real coil, where Q = ω₀L/r). | A real coil's resistance lowers f₀ below 1/(2π√(LC)) and gives a finite dynamic resistance RD = L/(rC); the ideal formula can fail when r is large. */
