/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - At resonance, a series RLC circuit stores energy in the inductor's magnetic field and the capacitor's electric field.
   - Q = 2π × Wmax / Wlost
   - Here wmax is the maximum energy stored in the circuit, in joules (J); Wlost is the energy turned into heat in R in one period, in J; Q has no unit.
   - For a series RLC at resonance, Wmax = ½ L Im² and Wlost = (Im²/2) R T, where Im is the peak current in A and T = 1/f₀ is the period in s.
   - Qseries = ω₀L / R = 1 / (ω₀CR)
   - Here ω₀ = 2πf₀ is the resonant angular frequency in rad/s; f₀ = 1/(2π√(LC)) is the resonant frequency in Hz.
   - For a parallel RLC near resonance, the same energy definition gives a reciprocal use of R.
   - Qparallel = R / (ω₀L) = ω₀CR
   - Here r is the shunt resistance in ohms (Ω); L and C are the same as above.
   - Bandwidth BW is the frequency range between the two half-power frequencies f₁ and f₂.
*/
