/* book Worked example 2: Q: A series RLC circuit has R = 10 Ω, L = 10 mH and C = 1 µF. Find the exact half-power frequencies and compare them with the f₀ ± BW/2 estimate.
   1. ω₀ = 1/√(LC) = 10 000 rad/s, f₀ = 1591.55 Hz, Q = ω₀L/R = 100/10 = 10.
   2. 1/(2Q) = 0.05 and √(1 + 1/(4Q²)) = √1.0025 = 1.001249.
   3. ω₁ = 10 000 × (1.001249 − 0.05) = 9512.5 rad/s, so f₁ = 1513.96 Hz.
   4. ω₂ = 10 000 × (1.001249 + 0.05) = 10 512.5 rad/s, so f₂ = 1673.11 Hz.
   5. BW = f₂ − f₁ = 159.15 Hz = f₀/Q, exactly. Check: √(f₁f₂) = √(1513.96 × 1673.11) = 1591.55 Hz = f₀.
   6. Estimate: f₀ ± BW/2 = 1511.97 Hz and 1671.13 Hz, about 2 Hz low on each side (0.13 %).
   Answer: f₁ = 1513.96 Hz and f₂ = 1673.11 Hz; the high-Q estimate is within 2 Hz. */
